  "transcript_segments": [
    {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 15.0,
      "text": "Dark the learn, let it sink, knuckles wide around the brink, leading twine, marked by mark, find the bottom in the dark."
    },
    {
      "start": 16.0,
      "end": 33.0,
      "text": "The fish has taught me, depth by touch, wet not to keep in careful count, no grand advice, no silver face."
    },
    {
      "start": 33.0,
      "end": 41.0,
      "text": "Just touch and patience, keep in place, I let it slip through thumb and tongue, felt the seagull cold and calm."
    },
    {
      "start": 41.0,
      "end": 47.0,
      "text": "Every feather took a thread, from things I thought were better dead."
    },
    {
      "start": 47.0,
      "end": 55.0,
      "text": "There was the island, there the pale, there the shirt that failed to sail, there the mouth that called it neat."
    },
    {
      "start": 55.0,
      "end": 70.0,
      "text": "While quietly teaching me to bleed, some depth sensor when you ask, some keep wearing their old masks, some return of grain of sand and ask, what else your grip is hiding."
    },
    {
      "start": 70.0,
      "end": 79.0,
      "text": "Sound it out, don't drag it up, not every bottom wants a cup, mark the depth and let it be."
    },
    {
      "start": 79.0,
      "end": 87.0,
      "text": "There are truths beneath the sea, sounded out, then give it slack, something speak by, not coming back."
    },
    {
      "start": 87.0,
      "end": 94.0,
      "text": "If I must cross what I don't see, let my hands remember me."
    },
    {
      "start": 95.0,
      "end": 114.0,
      "text": "The 20 marks the water cooled, at 30 I stopped feeling fooled, at 40 something and I knew the old day kept an undecided two."
    },
    {
      "start": 114.0,
      "end": 126.0,
      "text": "It wasn't just the anchor's pole, it wasn't only hunger's hollow, it was the fear of open drift, of having no excuse to lift."
    },
    {
      "start": 126.0,
      "end": 140.0,
      "text": "The line came back with clay and shells, small proof from where the quiet settled, I held it like a rough command and rinsed the clay from every knuckle it doesn't vanish when it's named."
    },
    {
      "start": 140.0,
      "end": 150.0,
      "text": "It doesn't owe you any change, but what you measure without pride can stop deciding from inside."
    },
    {
      "start": 150.0,
      "end": 158.0,
      "text": "Sound it out, don't drag it up, not every bottom wants a cup, mark the depth and let it be."
    },
    {
      "start": 158.0,
      "end": 166.0,
      "text": "There are truths beneath the sea, sounded out, then give it slack, something speak by, not coming back."
    },
    {
      "start": 166.0,
      "end": 173.0,
      "text": "If I must cross what I don't see, let my hands remember me."
    },
    {
      "start": 173.0,
      "end": 185.0,
      "text": "No, cure, no, anchor, no final word, I let the first be come up, sir, no, bless it, turn, no clean design, just wet, broke measure through my grip."
    },
    {
      "start": 185.0,
      "end": 207.0,
      "text": "And if I shake, let me shake, if I learn, let it take, mark by mark, not too fast, depth is not averted."
    },
    {
      "start": 215.0,
      "end": 233.0,
      "text": "Drop the line, let it sink, leave some room around the brink, lead in twine, palm and breath, I can cross without a myth."
    }
  ],
